1
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:17,480
Those who ceaselessly hone the art
of killing are known as masters.

2
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:22,157
These lethal abilities, dutifully
passed down through many generations,

3
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:25,200
have become what are
called modified bloodlines.

4
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:28,837
This is the story of one such master,

5
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:32,720
Hikaru Gero of the Poison Clan
and his greatest challenge yet,

6
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:34,180
to get married.

7
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:57,200
No mama, lots of time.

8
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:46,730
Kill or kiss Let's go!

9
00:01:47,726 --> 00:01:51,180
Let's go!

10
00:02:06,740 --> 00:02:08,840
Here's a photo of Toshiki Hanamaki.

11
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:14,100
He's the bug master and a long-time
colleague, and also my buddy. Oh, wow!

12
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:16,757
So this is a guy who's getting married?

13
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:18,760
He sure got that killer vibe!

14
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,706
I hope you have a great time!

15
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:24,117
Hey, Kinosaki.

16
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:26,788
Looks like there's also
a butterfly for you.

17
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:29,880
Dear Mei Kinosaki,

18
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:34,609
I hope you are faring well despite this
early summer heat we're experiencing.

19
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:35,830
Mr.

20
00:02:35,913 --> 00:02:37,477
Gato has informed me of your arrangement.

21
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:41,917
I cannot tell you how thankful I am you're
assisting with his search for a partner.

22
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,977
Your dedication and
selflessness are so admirable.

23
00:02:45,060 --> 00:02:47,997
I would be honored if you
would attend my humble wedding,

24
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:51,420
so I may be able to express
my gratitude in person.

25
00:02:51,980 --> 00:02:55,200
Yours truly, Toshiki Hanamaki, Bugmaster.

26
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:58,040
What a stand-up guy!

27
00:02:58,360 --> 00:03:00,837
I've never been invited
to a wedding before.

28
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:01,750
Please help.

29
00:03:01,833 --> 00:03:03,857
I want to make sure I'm dressed the part.

30
00:03:03,940 --> 00:03:06,580
After all, it is his special day. You bet!

31
00:03:06,820 --> 00:03:11,197
And a wedding is a great place to meet
new people, including potential paramours.

32
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:13,597
Mama's gonna need a brand new outfit, too.

33
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:15,033
Your treat, okie-dokie.

34
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:27,110
Uh!

35
00:03:27,193 --> 00:03:33,620
I was expecting a bug thing,
but he outdid himself.

36
00:03:33,940 --> 00:03:37,940
It looks like it was ripped straight
from the pages of a fairy tale.

37
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:46,810
Get out!

38
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:51,760
Is he dead?

39
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:54,980
Get out, that's not me!

40
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:58,066
You haven't been doing
too hot, huh, boss man?

41
00:03:58,360 --> 00:04:00,797
Leaning too hard on
your modified bloodline.

42
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:03,060
That was only a temporary pick-me-up.

43
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:06,600
Allow me to introduce you both.

44
00:04:07,220 --> 00:04:09,717
Kinosaki, this is Tsunagi,
the Needle Master.

45
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:11,877
He's a friend of mine,
like the Bug Master.

46
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:12,980
Happy to help.

47
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:15,080
Guess what, boys?

48
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,160
Ad made bank.

49
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:19,700
Who's up for Undeadsneyland this weekend?

50
00:04:20,060 --> 00:04:23,320
Will we get to meet the real
Undeadsney, Pa? Of course.

51
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:25,857
I'm planning the most optimal ride route.

52
00:04:25,940 --> 00:04:26,897
I leave it to you.

53
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:28,397
What a great dad, I think.

54
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:29,951
With three little clones.

55
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:34,457
If you're Kinosaki, that must mean you're
the big guy's marriage advisor, huh?

56
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:38,140
That's gotta be rough. I feel
for you. See? You get it.

57
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:43,717
We would like to welcome all of our honored
guests who have gathered here today.

58
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:46,388
The bride and groom
cannot thank you enough.

59
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:51,917
Now please join us as
we celebrate the union

60
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:55,300
between Toshiki Hanamaki
and Anna Kawakita.

61
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:06,980
We have to bring the underworld out
of the darkness and into the light.

62
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:09,064
The black market organ dealers,

63
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:11,077
all of the drug cartels.

64
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:13,400
We must join hands in unity.

65
00:05:14,220 --> 00:05:19,320
Ending this ridiculous forced isolation
once and for all has always been my dream.

66
00:05:27,580 --> 00:05:29,020
Glad you made it.

67
00:05:29,860 --> 00:05:33,457
I only showed up tonight because
you can't seem to take a hint.

68
00:05:33,540 --> 00:05:34,370
Listen,

69
00:05:34,453 --> 00:05:35,937
if you think getting on
my good side is going to

70
00:05:36,020 --> 00:05:38,317
win your family any favors
with my grandmother,

71
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:39,230
then you're...

72
00:05:41,540 --> 00:05:43,952
Sorry if I gave you the wrong impression.

73
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:46,900
I just wanted to have a drink together.

74
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:50,900
If you're up for it, Hikaru Gero.

75
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:56,660
Would you care to join me?

76
00:05:58,300 --> 00:06:01,860
Afraid it's non-alcoholic,
since you're underage.

77
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:05,580
Gero, did you hear that story?

78
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:07,460
Which one?

79
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,717
How the two of them first met.

80
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:13,506
Anna got into trouble while
mountain climbing and he saved her.

81
00:06:14,700 --> 00:06:15,935
Sounds just like him.

82
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:59,280
Kinosaki, do you think I'll ever
get to have a wedding this perfect?

83
00:07:00,060 --> 00:07:00,890
No question.

84
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:03,595
After all, you have me in your corner.

85
00:07:06,220 --> 00:07:07,760
Congrats, Toshiki.

86
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:25,240
Sure looks like you've got plenty of
happiness and love, don't you, Bug Master?

87
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:26,980
It ain't fair.

88
00:07:33,300 --> 00:07:36,797
Our couple met in the mountains,
and now spend their days camping.

89
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:38,917
They're both fans of hiking naturally,

90
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,537
but equally enjoy chatting
around the campfire.

91
00:07:41,620 --> 00:07:43,561
We'll take another Chateaubriand!

92
00:07:43,700 --> 00:07:46,417
And at night, while looking
up at the starry sky...

93
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:47,330
Get away!

94
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:49,797
Are you supposed to be
giving a big speech soon?

95
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:52,500
You'll have to cover for me! Oh, man?

96
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:53,960
Who's the spider?

97
00:07:55,320 --> 00:07:56,800
You said it, Juliet Jr.

98
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:59,277
You care about him just as much as I do,

99
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:02,654
and neither one of us want
anything to ruin his wedding.

100
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:07,017
I mean, this is the most
important day of Toshiki's life.

101
00:08:07,100 --> 00:08:07,930
Right.

102
00:08:09,740 --> 00:08:11,840
In exactly five minutes,

103
00:08:11,960 --> 00:08:15,920
all of you rush your assigned
entrances and kill whoever you want.

104
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:19,557
And remember, the more
stiffs, the bigger your bonus.

105
00:08:19,640 --> 00:08:23,405
As soon as Buggy and his master
friends start fighting back, go.

106
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:25,240
I'll take care of the rest.

107
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:29,957
While they're distracted, I'll
plant a fancy firework on the bride.

108
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:33,017
I bet she'll make a pretty
color when she goes off.

109
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:36,017
There's a picture that the
groom won't be able to forget.

110
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:37,480
That's my gift too

111
00:08:43,020 --> 00:08:47,860
Well, I guess that's what I get for
hiring mercs on the dark nav fine!

112
00:08:49,380 --> 00:08:51,262
Looks like it's time for plan B?

113
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:04,136
Firestorm Labyrinth!

114
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:06,600
Oh, look what you made me do.

115
00:09:06,900 --> 00:09:07,880
What a waste.

116
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:11,591
And here I was planning on
using those bombs on the guests.

117
00:09:11,940 --> 00:09:12,770
Woo!

118
00:09:13,620 --> 00:09:14,600
Can't be helped.

119
00:09:14,860 --> 00:09:16,797
Guess that's the way
the cookie goes kaboom.

120
00:09:16,880 --> 00:09:20,397
And besides, all I really care
about is paying back that Bugmaster.

121
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:24,280
The man responsible for stealing
the only true spark in my life.

122
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:25,930
That's right.

123
00:09:26,220 --> 00:09:29,760
Back in those days, I didn't
give a crap about anything.

124
00:09:30,380 --> 00:09:32,260
School, work, marriage.

125
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:35,128
I never felt there was
a point to any of it.

126
00:09:35,740 --> 00:09:39,840
Even when I ended up buried in
debt, it didn't seem to matter.

127
00:09:43,100 --> 00:09:45,100
Or when my payment was demanded,

128
00:09:45,340 --> 00:09:50,281
and it meant someone called the Puppet
Master turned me into a hitman for some gang.

129
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:53,140
All I could think was, whatever.

130
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:58,960
Well, Yamada, you're a new man.

131
00:09:59,500 --> 00:10:03,517
Miniature bombs have been surgically
planted in your wrist, ankles, and head.

132
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:06,140
In other words, you're permanently armed.

133
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:09,997
Press the switch in your back
tooth at the moment of impact.

134
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:13,660
The explosion will take out
your target and an extremity.

135
00:10:13,860 --> 00:10:15,820
A real explosion roulette.

136
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:21,440
As of this moment, your only purpose
in life is to go out with a bang.

137
00:10:27,740 --> 00:10:31,564
If things went sideways, I could
take myself out with the target.

138
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:33,717
For the first time in my life,

139
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:38,580
I felt the fire live within me, all
thanks to the explosion roulette.

140
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:45,800
Then he stole it from me.

141
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:05,430
Gotcha!

142
00:11:05,620 --> 00:11:09,796
At this range, setting off the bomb
in my brain will take him out, too!

143
00:11:10,100 --> 00:11:11,880
Talk about using my head!

144
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:16,980
I disarmed it for you.

145
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:19,672
You don't need to be afraid of dying now.

146
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:25,847
Just like that, it was over!

147
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:30,237
That inseparable freak took away my only
passion just to feel good about himself!

148
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:31,900
If he sold what I love,

149
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:35,477
haven't I also got the right to take
away what he values most in life?

150
00:11:35,560 --> 00:11:38,837
I got new limbs courtesy of the
puppet master as an advance,

151
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:41,517
made out like a bandit
doing loads of crap jobs,

152
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:45,920
all the while waiting for this day
to come, and you're not stopping me!

153
00:11:47,060 --> 00:11:49,440
Wait, that's right, you're already dead.

154
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:52,617
And thank you for being so understanding.

155
00:11:52,700 --> 00:11:56,757
I really appreciate this sushi.

156
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:58,100
That's a deal!

157
00:12:00,700 --> 00:12:01,530
Sorry.

158
00:12:01,613 --> 00:12:04,317
You say something doesn't matter.

159
00:12:04,400 --> 00:12:06,037
I don't know who you are.

160
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:09,157
But no decent person holds a
grudge against the bug master.

161
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:12,122
And we didn't hire a clown
for the entertainment.

162
00:12:15,300 --> 00:12:17,771
Now let's hear from a friend of the groom.

163
00:12:20,140 --> 00:12:24,611
Gedo officially owes me the most expensive
dinner in the history of dinners.

164
00:12:29,880 --> 00:12:31,620
It's really coming down, huh?

165
00:12:32,380 --> 00:12:35,204
Yeah, so much for a
gorgeous view of the sunset.

166
00:12:36,120 --> 00:12:38,797
Please welcome a dear
friend of the groom, Mr.

167
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:39,980
Hikaru Gedo.

168
00:12:41,020 --> 00:12:42,000
Or not.

169
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:44,917
Apologies, Gedo came down
with a case of stage fright.

170
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:48,417
But he prepared a speech he
asked me to read on his behalf.

171
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:50,200
My name's Mei Kinosaki.

172
00:12:57,480 --> 00:12:58,320
Hey, buddy!

173
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:00,951
Aren't you a mess, Kevin?

174
00:13:01,160 --> 00:13:03,880
So break out your modified
bloodline! Come on!

175
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:04,890
What's the deal?

176
00:13:04,973 --> 00:13:06,140
You scared? Let's go!

177
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,294
As if I'd waste it on the likes of you.

178
00:13:12,860 --> 00:13:16,617
Toshiki, Anna, congratulations
on such a wonderful wedding.

179
00:13:16,700 --> 00:13:21,524
If I'm being honest, that's not something
I imagined I would ever hear myself say.

180
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:23,940
My old friend.

181
00:13:24,660 --> 00:13:27,897
As you know, I'm also hoping
to walk down the aisle soon.

182
00:13:27,980 --> 00:13:30,560
And let me tell you, it's hard as hell.

183
00:13:33,220 --> 00:13:36,457
If only my younger self
could see me now, he'd say.

184
00:13:36,540 --> 00:13:38,775
Don't do it, you're wasting your time.

185
00:13:40,940 --> 00:13:42,100
But here I am.

186
00:13:42,580 --> 00:13:47,345
There's a reason I'm ready to embrace life
and open myself up to someone special.

187
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:51,220
Because I was lucky enough to meet you.

188
00:13:54,520 --> 00:13:58,097
Toshiki, when I was just some punk
kid going through the motions,

189
00:13:58,180 --> 00:14:00,420
why did you decide to care about me?

190
00:14:02,540 --> 00:14:05,187
On behalf of that kid,
I'd like to thank you.

191
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:07,460
If you weren't there.

192
00:14:09,280 --> 00:14:11,660
I'm sure I'd be lost.

193
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:26,435
It didn't matter what you were facing.

194
00:14:26,620 --> 00:14:30,796
You never let it stop you from reaching
out to someone who needed help.

195
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:33,637
That's what makes you my best friend.

196
00:14:33,720 --> 00:14:35,838
And the coolest guy I've ever known.

197
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:43,620
I don't want the memory of today
stained with your blood, so beat it.

198
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:47,700
Seems you're in a bit of trouble, Yamada.

199
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:49,820
I stand by my products.

200
00:14:50,480 --> 00:14:52,340
I'll release your limiters.

201
00:14:52,560 --> 00:14:55,940
Blow them all away with a
Typhoon-level blast wave.

202
00:15:03,660 --> 00:15:07,080
I've got a real big surprise
for you, Bud Master!

203
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:21,020
Damn it!

204
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:23,260
It ain't fair!

205
00:15:24,460 --> 00:15:27,997
You're deeper into the underworld
than a lonely hitman like me.

206
00:15:28,080 --> 00:15:32,021
A weapon of mass destruction more
dangerous than the exploding man.

207
00:15:33,260 --> 00:15:37,760
So how did you have it in
you to embrace me so gently?

208
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:41,080
Yamada, you're going the wrong way.

209
00:15:41,960 --> 00:15:43,957
Don't tell me you're...

210
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:49,500
Consider this my farewell gift!

211
00:15:51,860 --> 00:15:57,120
Lastly, Anna, it goes without saying,
but the moment that you found Toshiki,

212
00:16:01,020 --> 00:16:03,820
your happily ever after was guaranteed.

213
00:16:05,240 --> 00:16:06,080
The end.

214
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:08,212
Thank you for listening.

215
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:16,372
If you'd be so kind, please
take a look out of the window.

216
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:29,591
Toshiki, congratulations.

217
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:46,660
I want to thank you, Kinosaki.

218
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:50,852
Not just for the speech, but
for helping Gero find a wife.

219
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:52,360
It's no biggie.

220
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:56,457
My contributions are small potatoes
compared to all you've given him.

221
00:16:56,540 --> 00:17:00,599
I mean, even when Gero was a moody
teenager, you never left his side.

222
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:05,657
While that may be true, I'm the
one who should be thanking him.

223
00:17:05,740 --> 00:17:06,570
Huh?

224
00:17:06,653 --> 00:17:09,320
With the power dynamic
between our families,

225
00:17:09,620 --> 00:17:14,091
someone in his position shouldn't be
my friend, much less attend my wedding.

226
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:15,520
I'm fortunate.

227
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:17,500
What power dynamic?

228
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:22,565
I was kind of under the impression both
of you were masters and there wasn't one.

229
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:29,080
The Hanamaki Bugmasters
started with venomous insects,

230
00:17:29,280 --> 00:17:31,537
the Tsunagi Needlemasters with poison.

231
00:17:31,620 --> 00:17:36,600
There are other masters that specialize
in diseases and physical ailments.

232
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:38,457
But our branch families,

233
00:17:38,540 --> 00:17:44,320
we recognize the Poison Clan as our ancestors
and answer to them without question.

234
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:47,900
There are only five great
families at the top.

235
00:17:48,940 --> 00:17:51,680
The Gero family, the Arima,

236
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:56,560
the Dogo, the Kirishima, and the Nasuka.

237
00:17:57,900 --> 00:18:01,817
The entire society of masters
is made up of their families,

238
00:18:01,900 --> 00:18:04,357
branch families, and their offshoots.

239
00:18:04,440 --> 00:18:07,037
Clans not related to them are rare.

240
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:11,537
If one of the great families told
a branching one their time was up,

241
00:18:11,620 --> 00:18:14,117
they would off themselves
without complaint.

242
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:16,100
That's how low we are.

243
00:18:18,380 --> 00:18:20,077
Listen carefully, Toshiki.

244
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:24,440
Our family we live only thanks
to the ghetto's good graces.

245
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:27,390
For centuries,

246
00:18:27,473 --> 00:18:30,557
the heads of the five great households
have been toying with human lives.

